This study documents a previously unreported columnar growth form of starlet corals (Siderastreidae:
Siderastrea
) on shallow-mesophotic, turbid-zone reefs of the Abrolhos Bank, southwestern Atlantic. Photogrammetry and computed tomography reveal that these multi-centennial, continuous colonies likely represent a vertical escape strategy to cope with sediment dynamics, while also constituting valuable archives of past environmental variability.
